+Self-hosted WebSockets were chosen over five-second HTTPS polling and hosted realtime services. Polling was rejected because its cursor-query model adds repeated read load and inherent lag. Hosted realtime was rejected to avoid recurring fees, provider coupling, and credential management. Self-hosted sockets accept the operational burden of connection capacity and reconnect logic in exchange for fast updates without a vendor bill.
+
+Delivery, change storage, and browser recovery are designed together around this choice. The change store provides revision history and an outbox for publication replay. Delivery manages socket sessions, handles reconnect/catch-up, and publishes from the outbox. Browser sync uses the socket subscription model with explicit reconnect and catch-up logic.
 
